### Sample API requests and responses
###
### Every response below is REAL output captured from a live run against
### Gemini (gemini-flash-latest / gemini-flash-lite-latest). Long replies are
### truncated with an ellipsis; nothing else is edited.
###
### Replay them yourself:  uvicorn app.main:app --reload

### 1. Create a user profile
#    Zodiac is DERIVED from dob — it is never accepted as input.
POST http://localhost:8000/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "user-123",
  "name": "Rahul",
  "dob": "1995-08-15",
  "tob": "09:30",
  "birth_place": "Delhi",
  "language": "en"
}

# --> 201
# {
#   "user_id": "user-123",
#   "name": "Rahul",
#   "dob": "1995-08-15",
#   "tob": "09:30",
#   "birth_place": "Delhi",
#   "language": "en",
#   "zodiac": "Leo",
#   "element": "fire",
#   "missing_fields": []
# }

### 2. First message — states a goal worth remembering
#    Nothing is in the graph yet, so retrieval_strategy ends in :empty.
#    The goal is extracted AFTER this reply is sent.
POST http://localhost:8000/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "user-123",
  "session_id": "session-456",
  "message": "My name is Rahul. I was born on 15 August 1995 in Delhi. I'm planning to switch jobs next year."
}

# --> 200
# {
#   "response": "Planning a career move next year aligns well with your natural drive to step into spaces where your efforts are genuinely visible and valued. You do your best work when you have a healthy degree of creative ownership and recognition, so make sure this transition isn't just a lateral jump for a quick …",
#   "user_id": "user-123",
#   "session_id": "session-456",
#   "context_used": [
#     "user_profile"
#   ],
#   "retrieval_strategy": "graph:career:empty",
#   "degraded": false,
#   "degraded_reason": null
# }

### 3. Uses the stored goal
#    context_used now carries goal:career-change — the proof that
#    selection pulled it out of the Shared Brain.
POST http://localhost:8000/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "user-123",
  "session_id": "session-456",
  "message": "What should I focus on for my career?"
}

# --> 200
# {
#   "response": "Right now, your main focus should be on building clear professional visibility and ownership. With your fiery, Leo-driven energy, you do your best work when you aren't hidden in the background or stuck under heavy micromanagement. Aim to establish a distinct personal brand—become the go-to person fo …",
#   "user_id": "user-123",
#   "session_id": "session-456",
#   "context_used": [
#     "user_profile",
#     "short_term_context",
#     "goal:career-change"
#   ],
#   "retrieval_strategy": "graph:career",
#   "degraded": false,
#   "degraded_reason": null
# }

### 4. Follow-up — short-term context only
#    retrieval_strategy is short_term_only: the graph was NOT queried.
POST http://localhost:8000/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "user-123",
  "session_id": "session-456",
  "message": "Why do you say that?"
}

# --> 200
# {
#   "response": "It comes down to your core astrological makeup. Being born under the sign of Leo, a fire sign ruled by the Sun, your professional drive is closely tied to pride in your craft and a need for genuine self-expression. When people with this placement are tucked away in repetitive, behind-the-scenes role …",
#   "user_id": "user-123",
#   "session_id": "session-456",
#   "context_used": [
#     "user_profile",
#     "short_term_context"
#   ],
#   "retrieval_strategy": "short_term_only",
#   "degraded": false,
#   "degraded_reason": null
# }

### 5. NEW session — must recall from the Shared Brain
#    Different session_id, so short-term is empty. The goal still arrives,
#    and the reply names the target year it stored earlier.
POST http://localhost:8000/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "user-123",
  "session_id": "session-999",
  "message": "What do you remember about my career goals?"
}

# --> 200
# {
#   "response": "You’ve shared that you are aiming for a significant career change, with your sights set on 2027. With your natural Leo drive, it makes complete sense that you are looking for a path that offers genuine visibility, creative ownership, and work you can feel truly recognized for. \n\nHaving a target a co …",
#   "user_id": "user-123",
#   "session_id": "session-999",
#   "context_used": [
#     "user_profile",
#     "goal:career-change"
#   ],
#   "retrieval_strategy": "graph:recall",
#   "degraded": false,
#   "degraded_reason": null
# }

### 6. Inspect the Shared Brain
###    Superseded facts are included on purpose — the audit trail is the feature.
GET http://localhost:8000/users/user-123/brain

# {
#   "user_id": "user-123",
#   "profile": {
#     "user_id": "user-123",
